 "notes": {
  "fAbout": {
   "x": 1280,
   "y": 0,
   "w": 460,
   "fill": "pink",
   "size": "m",
   "page": "foundations",
   "text": "LensLayer mobile · design system\n\nScene: a procurement or legal lead checking a renewal deadline on their phone between meetings, in daylight, needing to confirm a date and assign an owner in under a minute. Light by default; dark follows the phone.\n\nColour: restrained. Warm paper neutrals, charcoal for primary actions, deep rose for links and the active tab. The four pastels mark destinations only (butter contracts, pink decisions, olive actions, blue dates). Risk uses red/amber/green badges with words, never colour alone.\n\nType: Figtree, the same family as the web workspace. Tabular figures for dates and money.\n\nAnchors: Apple Settings (grouped lists), Things 3 (agenda and completion), Linear mobile (calm density).\n\nAll companies, people and contracts on this canvas are fictional."
  },
  "sRow1": {
   "x": 0,
   "y": -300,
   "text": "Launch & sign in",
   "kind": "title1",
   "maxW": 3210,
   "page": "splash"
  },
  "sRow2": {
   "x": 0,
   "y": 964,
   "text": "Recovery, verification & sessions",
   "kind": "title1",
   "maxW": 3210,
   "page": "splash"
  },
  "sNote": {
   "x": 3300,
   "y": 0,
   "w": 420,
   "fill": "blue",
   "size": "m",
   "page": "splash",
   "text": "Engineering note\n\nLensLayer signs in through Auth0. These screens are the target look for Auth0’s hosted Universal Login (branded to match), shown inside a secure in-app browser sheet, so the app never handles the password itself. Face ID unlock and Session ended are native app screens."
  },
